# A CSS file whose Hugo template code lives inside a CSS comment, so Hugo can
# derive the variables at build time. Prettier's CSS parser crashes on the
# template actions, and renaming it so the go-template parser picks it up makes
# things worse: that parser reflows the comment and drops the :root block. There
# is no extension or edit that makes this file safe to format.
assets/css/variables.css

# A Hugo template that emits the FlexSearch index, so it opens with a template
# action and is not valid JSON. Renaming it so prettier skips it is not an
# option either: Hugo derives the media type from the extension, and a non-.json
# source leaves the generated file with no mimetype, which fails minification.
assets/json/search-data.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Hugo templates
#
# prettier-plugin-go-template cannot format Hugo templates without changing what
# they render. Three failures, each reproduced by building the site and diffing
# all 302 pages:
#
#   1. It reflows a single-line attribute across lines, and the newlines land
#      inside the attribute value. `aria-expanded="{{ if $open }}true{{ else }}
#      false{{ end }}"` renders as aria-expanded=" false " on every collapsible
#      sidebar section, breaking ARIA on 259 of 302 pages.
#   2. It moves the closing `-}}` of a multi-line `{{- /* ... */ -}}` comment onto
#      its own line, splitting `*/ -}}` into something Hugo cannot parse. ~94
#      templates carry such comments.
#   3. It drops significant spaces next to template actions, merging CSS class
#      names and deleting separators (see the title separator in head.html).
#
# Formatting these by hand where it mattered is what the fixes above do; running
# the formatter over all of them is not safe.
layouts/**/*.html
docs/layouts/**/*.html

# ------------------------------------------------------------- Markdown content
#
# Prettier reads the indented `>}}` that closes a multi-line shortcode call as a
# blockquote marker and rewrites it to `> }}`, after which Hugo fails with
# "unrecognized character in shortcode action". Avoiding it would mean putting
# every multi-line shortcode call in content on a single line.
docs/content/**

# ----------------------------------------------------------- Generated / vendored
#
# Build output and third-party bundles: regenerated or copied verbatim, so
# formatting them is churn at best and expands minified bundles at worst.
assets/css/compiled/
assets/js/vendor/
docs/hugo_stats.json
docs/public/

# ------------------------------------------------- templates that cannot be formatted
#
# Each of these opens (or interleaves) a multi-line doc comment whose surrounding
# whitespace is trimmed by the comment's own `-}}`, and whose neighbour is literal
# HTML rather than another action. Prettier splits `*/ -}}` on such a comment, and
# every way of avoiding that leaks whitespace into the output instead:
#   * the no-trim `{{/* ... */}}` form emits the whitespace the comment used to trim;
#   * an ignore fence must also use the no-trim form (the plugin does not recognise
#     `{{- /* prettier-ignore-start */ -}}`), so the fence leaks in its place.
# Nothing adjacent can absorb it, so these keep their doc comments and exact output.
# Every other template under layouts/ is formatted.
layouts/_partials/blog/identity.html
layouts/_partials/blog/rail.html
layouts/_partials/blog/widget-heading.html
layouts/_partials/components/codeblock.html
layouts/_partials/scripts/typeit.html
layouts/_partials/scripts/youtube-lite.html
layouts/_shortcodes/chart.html
layouts/_shortcodes/email.html
layouts/_shortcodes/filetree/container.html
